ollowers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-10-26T14:27:38Z","updated_at":"2024-10-26T14:27:38Z","body":"I wonder if the original logic was designed to return a relative path on purpose. The rationale is that when trying to `load()` files from the exported project, you would use a relative path that assumes CWD is the project root.\r\n\r\nThat said, I think this new logic makes more sense ultimately. However, I wouldn't be surprised if it breaks a project out there somewhere…","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2439602150/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2439986252","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98460#issuecomment-2439986252","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98460","id":2439986252,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6RbzxM","user":{"login":"TML233","id":19572238,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NTcyMjM4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19572238?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TML233","html_url":"https://github.com/TML233","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TML233/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TML233/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TML233/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TML233/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TML233/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TML233/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TML233/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TML233/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TML233/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-10-27T12:02:36Z","updated_at":"2024-10-27T12:02:36Z","body":"> I wonder if the original logic was designed to return a relative path on purpose. The rationale is that when trying to `load()` files from the exported project, you would use a relative path that assumes CWD is the project root.\n> \n> \n> \n> That said, I think this new logic makes more sense ultimately. However, I wouldn't be surprised if it breaks a project out there somewhere…\n\nWell, we can leave the old one as is and create a new one that returns an empty string when failed. I think the old behavior is just muffling the errors, since if you want to globalize a path, you should get a globalized path or just fail completely.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2439986252/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]